DECISION
==============================================================================
  SCORE ALL 5,041, MARK THE 3,789. The ungauged subset is not
  materially out-of-distribution -- worst feature 0.158%, against
  0.008% on the gauge grid itself. But it is still unverifiable:
  no IMD gauge means no label ever existed there, so nothing about
  those points has been or can be scored. They get a DISTINCT
  STATE, 'outside the verified domain', and are excluded from
  every headline count.

  IN-RANGE IS NOT VERIFIED. This check says the live features sit
  inside the training hull; it says NOTHING about whether the model
  is accurate there, because no truth has ever existed at those
  points. Do not let 'in distribution' be read as 'validated'.

